  "description": "WIGQIM crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P a -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H164 Eu8 O26. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2K (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2F (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3F (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3K (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.641-5.281 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.64-164.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Hx[Eu8O6(OC6H3Me2-2,6)12(OiPr)8]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OiPr (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
